Z||000001||falconhulk||09-17-2001||12:37 PM||||This is definitely a to much fuel problem.  The secondary are opening to soon.  Vacuum secondary are the best as opposed to mechanical secondary or double pumpers.  This is a common problem in carbed cars.  I have a carbed mustang that I went from a Holley mech. to a carter vacuum and it fixed the problem.  The secondary don't open unless they are needed.  For normal driving the car behaves itself.  When you stomp it the beast awakens!!  For vacuum secondary the engine has to be under load and you cannot open them by just stomping on the gas with it in park.  With mech secondary they will open and screw up the mixture.  If you have mech secondary and want to stay with them even rejetting may not help.  You may have to go to a smaller carb.  If you have a vac secondary then rejetting will definitely help.  I would suggest going with a vacuum carb for any performance/street car.<p>[This message has been edited by falconhulk (edited 09-17-2001).]||||reg||1
